<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wassenaar Agreement</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1982">1982</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wassenaar Agreement was concluded on 24 November 1982 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> employers' organisations and trade unions, at a time of high unemployment. Unions accepted wage moderation in return for shorter working hours and efforts to create jobs. It is regarded as the start of the consensual 'polder model' credited with the strong Dutch economic recovery of the 1990s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wassenaar-agreement.jpg" alt="Wassenaar Agreement" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Croes / Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:V.l.n.r._Van_Eijkelenburg_(NCW),_Van_Veen_(VNO),_Kok_(FNV)_en_Harm_van_der_Meule,_Bestanddeelnr_932-4158.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
